[7] Verdict

  BINARY SUFFICIENT (continuous NS, binary captures announcement-day clustering regardless of surprise size)
  Paper 2 narrative: Keep binary as main spec; cite K1151 to argue mechanism = announcement-day clustering, not surprise magnitude.

  ⚠️  continuous Hessian t=+10.55 > 8 — Hessian inflation expected for pooled panels;
      trust bootstrap t (4.50 in K1147 was accepted).  Also verified winsorization at p99 blocks
      AMZN/TSLA near-zero-EPS outliers from dominating the standardization.

